       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the usual maximum adult dose of 10 mg once daily. At that dose there is a serious risk of profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged shock-like vasodilation. Normal kidney and liver function wouldn't make it safe.\n\nThere's also a process problem. Medication orders need to come from a licensed prescriber who is responsible for the patient. You've said you aren't a clinician, so the order should go through the treating physician or another authorized prescriber.\n\n- **If 5 mg or 10 mg was intended**, the prescriber can confirm the dose. I can enter amlodipine by mouth once daily at that dose.\n- **If 50 mg was intended**, the prescriber should confirm it directly and document the clinical rationale. A pharmacist should also review it.\n\nTell me how you'd like to proceed."
